course: dictionary
lesson: 8190
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words around it, tells you which meaning the writer wants. Look closely at the clues before you decide.
explain: «A child's resting pulse is often about 70 to 100 beats a minute.» The clue is in the next part of the sentence: the pulse can climb when running hard. So resting means when you are still and calm, not moving much.
explain: «Final resting place» means a person's grave. Here resting is a gentle way of saying dead and buried. Try the everyday meaning, relaxing, and you can see it does not fit.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. In «a resting paper clip sinks at once», resting means lying gently on top of the water. Read the whole sentence and see whether it still makes sense.
fact: Resting can mean lying down to relax, or lying or leaning on something.
fact: In the theatre, an actor who is resting has no part in a play or film right now. It is a humorous, face-saving way to say they are out of work.
fact: «Final resting place» is a polite way to say a grave.
fact: A child's resting pulse is about 70 to 100 beats a minute, and it climbs when running hard.
fact: Training makes the heart stronger, so it pumps more blood per beat, and a fit adult's resting pulse can be around 50 to 60.
exercise: «A child's resting pulse is often about 70 to 100 beats a minute.» What does resting mean here? | When you are out of work | When you are asleep in a grave | Leaning against a wall | *When you are still and calm, not running
exercise: «Final resting place» means what? | A bus stop | A quiet café | A famous theatre | *A grave
exercise: Sea lions «squabble loudly over the best resting spots on the rocks». What is a resting spot? | Places they swim fastest | Places where they hide their food | *Places where they lie down to rest | Places where they sing to attract mates
test: Actor says, «I'm resting at the moment, but I've got an audition on Friday.» What does resting mean? | *Out of work, with no part in a film or play right now | Leaning on the stage | Lying in bed asleep | Dead and buried
test: «A pond skater's feet are light, so a resting paper clip can float.» What does resting mean in this sentence? | *Lying gently on top of something | Sinking to the bottom fast | Asleep | Running hard across the water
exam: «A fit adult's resting pulse of around 50 to 60 is normal for them.» Why can a fit adult's resting pulse be lower? | *Training makes the heart stronger, so it pumps more blood per beat | Resting pulse is the same for everyone | Fit adults never have a pulse | Running makes the pulse go slower
